{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Button component (1:28):\n- 196×58, white fill, dark stroke (#161513 ~ rgb(0.086, 0.082, 0.075) = #161513), corner radius 100 (pill), auto-layout horizontal\n- Text: Poppins SemiBold 16, color #161513\n- This is the \"default\" button — likely a light button. Note the source kit is dark mode.\n\nDesign system decisions (my own):\n- Page background: #0F0F13 or similar very dark. Let me define:\n  - bg/page: #0D0D12 (near black)\n  - surface: #16161D\n  - surface-2: #1D1D26\n  - border: #2A2A35\n  - text primary: #FFFFFF\n  - text secondary: #B8B8C4 (gray)\n  - accent orange: #D5491D\n  - accent blue: #1373D1\n  - dark ink for light surfaces: #161513\n\nType scale (Poppins):\n- Display/Hero H1: 56 SemiBold\n- H2 section: 40 SemiBold\n- Card title: 24 SemiBold\n- Body: 16 Regular / Medium\n- Small: 14 Regular\n- Caption/eyebrow: 14 SemiBold, letter-spacing\n\nSpacing: 8-pt grid; page container 1120-1200 wide centered (1440 - 160 margins each side = 1120). Actually with 1440 wide, margins of 160 → content 1120. Or 120 margins → 1200. I'll use 1200 content width with 120 side margins? The original ABM portfolio (this is based on a known \"ABM signature portfolio\" design) uses wide margins. Let me use content width 1136 with 152 margins... simpler: container = 1200, margins 120.\n\nSections:\n1. Header (sticky look): height 96. Left: Logo_ABM signature (white). Right: nav Home / Projects / Experience / Contact. Current: Home (orange or accent color + maybe underline dot). Nav item components: Nav_Item with states Default / Current / Hover.\n2. Hero: two-column: left text (H1 \"I do code and make content about it!\", bio paragraph, buttons \"Get In Touch\" (primary, orange fill) and \"Download CV\" (secondary, outline)); right: avatar photo. Maybe decorative accents.\n3. Tech stack: eyebrow \"EXPERIENCE WITH\" + row of 5 logos (recolored to white/gray).\n4. Projects: H2 \"Projects\" + 2 cards (HTML TUTORIAL, CSS TUTORIAL), each with photo, \"CLICK HERE TO VISIT\" caption, title, arrow icon.\n5. Experience: H2 \"Experience\" + 3 entries, each with initials mark (S, MS, OC), role+company, dates, description.\n6. Contact footer: H2 \"Contact\", bio text (the \"Seasoned Full Stack...\" copy), email abm@example.com with Icon_Mail, social logos Instagram/X/YouTube. Then bottom footer bar with logo + copyright maybe.\n\nComponents to create in workspace:\n- Button (variant components): Button/Primary, Button/Secondary, + hover states? Brief says \"Design all other states\". I can create component sets with variants: Button with property Type=Primary/Secondary, State=Default/Hover. That's nice for \"State design\".\n- Nav_Item: variants State=Default/Current (and maybe Hover).\n- Header component (uses logo + nav instances).\n- Section_Heading maybe.\n- Tech_Logo_Item.\n- Project_Card.\n- Experience_Entry (or Company_Mark + Experience_Item).\n- Company_Mark (S, MS, OC) — as components.\n- Social_Link.\n- Contact_Block.\n- Footer.\n\nTo keep it manageable, I'll create components on the workspace page in a \"Components\" area to the left/right of the main frame, then compose the main frame with instances.\n\nImportant plugin API details:\n- The media components are in this same file, so I can create instances of them directly via createInstance on the COMPONENT nodes (3:4 etc. are symbols = components). Logo_ABM 3:4, Photo_Avatar 3:13, Photo_Project_CSS 3:14, Photo_Project_HTML 3:15, Logo_CSS3 3:5, Logo_HTML5 3:6, Logo_JavaScript 3:8, Logo_Nextjs 3:9, Logo_React 3:10, Logo_Instagram 3:7, Logo_X 3:11, Logo_YouTube 3:12, Icon_Arrow_Up_Right 3:2, Icon_Mail 3:3.\n- Recoloring third-party logos: they're supplied in #1A1A1F. I need to recolor to white/light for dark page. I can clone the symbol and override fills, or instance + set fills on vector children. With instances, I can set individual child fills via node.children traversal. Simpler: clone the component node and recolor vectors in the clone, then turn into my own component. But \"use them as instances\" is instructed. I can create an instance and set fills on its children (instance children allow fill overrides). Let me do instance.recursive override of fills for vector/text children. That keeps them as instances (good for \"component reuse\" evaluation).\n- Fonts: Poppins — need loadFontAsync for each style used: Regular, Medium, SemiBold, Bold. The gotcha says for Inter the style is \"Semi Bold\", but for Poppins it's \"SemiBold\" (confirmed by the Button text fontName: {family: \"Poppins\", style: \"SemiBold\"}).\n- Prototype: nav scroll interactions. The frame is a single page; sections are at different Y offsets. Prototype interactions: on click of nav item → \"Scroll to\" node? In plugin API, Interaction with action type \"SCROLL_TO\"? Actually there's action type { type: \"NODE\", destinationId, navigation: \"SCROLL\" }? Let me recall: Figma plugin API prototyping: \n  - new Interaction? In plugin API: node.reactio... Actually `Reaction` objects: { trigger: {type: \"CLICK\"}, action: { type: \"NODE\", destinationId: \"...\", navigation: \"NAVIGATE\" | \"SCROLL\" | \"CHANGE_TO\", transition: ..., } }. Yes — Reaction: node.reactions = [{ trigger: {type: 'Click'}, action: { type: 'NODE', destinationId: nodeId, navigation: 'SCROLL' } }]. For SCROLL navigation, transition is not needed I think. Let me set reactions on nav item components' instances? Reactions on instances... The nav items are components with variants; prototype interactions on component (main) apply to instances. I can set reactions on the Nav_Item main components: Current state's Home scrolls to hero? Hmm — but each instance in the header points to a different section. Reactions set on the main component would scroll all instances to the same destination. Better: set reactions directly on the instances in the header component. Instances can have reactions? In Figma, interactions can be added to instance sublayers (overrides). Plugin API: setting node.reactions on a node inside an instance — I believe it's allowed (it's an override) as long as the instance allows overrides. Actually reactions on instance children are supported as prototype overrides.\n\nAlternative simpler approach that definitely works: put nav items as instances, then set reactions on each instance child. If that fails, fallback: set reactions on the text/instance wrapper frame directly.\n\nActually, since \"Navigation items scroll to sections\" is the required prototype flow, I'll do:\n- In Header component: nav = 4 Nav_Item instances. Set reactions on each instance: click → scroll to section frame/anchor.\n- Sections need to be named frames (e.g., \"Home\", \"Projects\", \"Experience\", \"Contact\") within 01_Home so scroll destinations work. I'll create section frames as direct children of 01_Home: Hero section (Home anchor), Projects, Experience, Contact.\n\nScroll action: { type: \"NODE\", destinationId: id, navigation: \"SCROLL\" }. \n\nAlso hover state: brief says design hover states. I'll create variant states for Button (Default/Hover) and Nav_Item (Default/Current/Hover?). Also could add prototype \"mouse enter → change to hover variant\" interactions for the header button instances. The evaluation says \"State design (current nav item, hover)\". I'll create hover variants and optionally wire mouse-enter/leave interactions on instances in 01_Home. Let me wire at least the main buttons: ON HOVER change to variant hover. Trigger type \"MOUSE_ENTER\"/\"MOUSE_LEAVE\". Action: { type: \"CHANGE_TO\", destinationId: variantId, transition: {...} }. For CHANGE_TO, destinationId must be the specific variant component id.\n\nLet me plan colors precisely:\n\nDesign tokens:\n- bg-page: #0C0C10 (r 0.047, g 0.047, b 0.063)\n- bg-surface: #14141A\n- bg-card: #17171E\n- border: #26262E\n- border-subtle: #1F1F27\n- text-primary: #FFFFFF\n- text-secondary: #A3A3B2\n- text-muted: #6E6E7E\n- accent-orange: #D5491