e (allowed). No size change → all ~18px. Good.\n\nWait — nested swap: I'd rather use fills-override approach again (safe). So Social_Button default contains Instagram; instances override nested fills to #E8E8EE (already that color from component) — Instagram default needs no change; X/YouTube: fills override only. \n\nYouTube at 20×15 vs Instagram 18×18 — visually fine.\n\nFooter_Bar component (-1800, 2450): vertical, gap 28, width 1160 fixed:\n- divider rect 1160×1 #1E1E26\n- row: horizontal space-between, counter CENTER, width STRETCH: logo instance rescale 0.35 → 59×33.6; copyright text \"© 2026 ABM. All rights reserved.\" 14 Regular #6E6E7E.\n\nContact frame: paddingTop 110, gap 56 between block and footer bar? Footer bar bottom padding 48. Structure:\n- Contact frame: vertical, counter CENTER, paddingTop 110, paddingLeft 140, paddingRight 140, paddingBottom 48, itemSpacing 64:\n  - Contact_Block instance\n  - Footer_Bar instance (layoutAlign STRETCH — width 1160).\n\nThen home bottom done. \n\nAfter that: reactions (step 7):\n- Nav items in header component (8:15 Home current, 8:18 Projects, 8:21 Experience, 8:24 Contact): click → scroll to hero/projects/exp/contact frames.\n  Destinations: hero 11:28, projects 13:71, exp 14:75, contact (new id).\n  Wait — nav items are nested in header COMPONENT; the instance in 01_Home (11:11) inherits reactions. Set reactions on nested instances inside the component 8:12. Try node.reactions setter.\n- Hover wiring:\n  - Nav default items: MOUSE_ENTER → Nav_Item Hover variant (8:5); MOUSE_LEAVE → Default (8:2). Destination for CHANGE_TO must be variant component ids.\n  - Hero buttons: btnP (7:2 instance) MOUSE_ENTER → 7:4; LEAVE → 7:2. btnS → 7:8 / 7:6.\n- Also project card hover? Could add subtle: card instances MOUSE_ENTER → CHANGE_TO... no hover variant of card; skip.\n\nScroll action format: {type:'NODE', destinationId, navigation:'SCROLL', transition:{type:'SMART_ANIMATE', duration:0.8, easing:{type:'EASE_OUT'}}}? Hmm —