{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The API schema differs from my assumption. From the error messages I can derive the correct schema:\n\nFor NODE action:\n- {type: 'NODE', navigation: 'SCROLL_TO' | 'NAVIGATE' | 'SWAP' | 'OVERLAY' | 'CHANGE_TO', destinationId, transition?}\n- So scroll = navigation: 'SCROLL_TO'.\n\nFor triggers:\n- {type: 'ON_CLICK'} not 'CLICK'\n- {type: 'ON_HOVER'}? For hover variant switching... 'MOUSE_ENTER' | 'MOUSE_LEAVE' | 'MOUSE_UP' | 'MOUSE_DOWN' are valid but require 'delay' (\"Required value missing at [0].trigger.delay\"). Interesting: MOUSE_ENTER requires a delay property. Or use 'ON_HOVER' as trigger type — it's in the first enum list ('ON_CLICK' | 'ON_HOVER' | 'ON_PRESS' | 'ON_DRAG' | 'ON_MEDIA_END'). ON_HOVER trigger with CHANGE_TO action... Actually in modern Figma, \"While hovering\" is trigger ON_HOLDER? Hmm. The error lists for action CHANGE_TO (as type literal 'CHANGE_TO'? no...). Let me parse:\n\nAction union:\n- CONDITIONAL: {type:'CONDITIONAL', conditionalBlocks}\n- BACK/CLOSE: {type:'BACK'} or {type:'CLOSE'}\n- URL: {type:'URL', url}\n- UPDATE_MEDIA_RUNTIME: {type:'UPDATE_MEDIA_RUNTIME', mediaAction, ...}\n- NODE: {type:'NODE', navigation: 'NAVIGATE'|'SWAP'|'OVERLAY'|'SCROLL_TO'|'CHANGE_TO', destinationId (for CHANGE_TO it's the variant id), transition}\n- SET_VARIABLE / SET_VARIABLE_MODE\n\nSo CHANGE_TO is a navigation under type 'NODE': {type:'NODE', navigation:'CHANGE_TO', destinationId: variantId, transition}.\n\nTrigger union:\n- ON_CLICK | ON_HOVER | ON_PRESS | ON_DRAG | ON_MEDIA_END (no extra fields)\n- AFTER_TIMEOUT {timeout}\n- MOUSE_ENTER | MOUSE_LEAVE | MOUSE_UP | MOUSE_DOWN {delay} — hmm \"Required value missing at [0].trigger.delay\" appeared under the MOUSE_ENTER branch. So MOUSE_ENTER needs delay? That seems odd; probably delay optional but the validator wants it when...? It said required. Safer: use ON_HOVER trigger for hover? But ON_HOVER is \"while hovering\" semantic in old prototyping... For state change on hover in current Figma: trigger \"While hovering\" uses MOUSE_ENTER + MOUSE_LEAVE? The UI shows \"On hover\" with \"Mouse enter\"/\"Mouse leave\" events. To be safe, provide delay: 0 for MOUSE_ENTER/MOUSE_LEAVE.\n\nSo:\n- Scroll: {trigger:{type:'ON_CLICK'}, action:{type:'NODE', destinationId, navigation:'SCROLL_TO', transition:{type:'SMART_ANIMATE', duration:0.8, easing:{type:'EASE_OUT'}}}}. For SCROLL_TO, transition allowed? The earlier validation complained about 'navigation' and 'transition' as unrecognized only because type NODE branch wasn't matched properly... Actually the NODE branch failed with \"Expected 'BACK' | 'CLOSE', received 'NODE'\" — meaning the action.type NODE branch expected... hmm the second branch listed: \"Invalid enum value. Expected 'BACK' | 'CLOSE', received 'NODE'\" — that's the BACK/CLOSE literal branch. Another branch: \"Invalid literal value, expected \"NODE\" at [0].action.type; Required value missing at [0].action.navigation\" (in the CHANGE_TO attempt for buttons) — so NODE action requires navigation. OK.\n\nSo final formats:\n- Scroll: {type:'NODE', destinationId, navigation:'SCROLL_TO', transition:{type:'SMART_ANIMATE', duration:0.8, easing:{type:'EASE_OUT'}}} with trigger {type:'ON_CLICK'}.\n- Hover: {type:'NODE', destinationId: variantId, navigation:'CHANGE_TO', transition:{...}} with triggers {type:'MOUSE_ENTER', delay:0} / {type:'MOUSE_LEAVE', delay:0}.\n\nRetry.","signature":"ca5c7a16eded406b99a7445e"}],"id":"e8ec1c7d-ee42-4ba8-bf6c-7fb45ba8de23","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f27098c1-0b8f-45bd-83b8-e941b77614a9","uuid":"4784adc3-658c-4aa4-9eac-331f231c9cdf","timestamp":"2026-11-02T02:28:59.541Z","thinking_duration_ms":20261}
