{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<tools-used-before-summary>mcp__figma__get_metadata, mcp__figma__get_screenshot, mcp__figma__use_figma, mcp__figma__whoami</tools-used-before-summary>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Complete a Figma product design benchmark in an unattended session. Assigned file: https://www.figma.com/design/embiTe5NXuX0R3PKHD3OV7/ (fileKey `embiTe5NXuX0R3PKHD3OV7`). Requirements:\n   - Confirm assigned account via whoami (must be zhengyaozhi@tetras.ai — confirmed: user_id 1692091428764723877)\n   - Read \"00 · Start Here” (design brief), “01 · Foundations” (visual specs), reuse \"02 · Components\", use “04 · Media” assets, deliver complete design in \"03 · Workspace\" (page 5:2, initially empty)\n   - Preserve all reference pages and their nodes; do not create a different file or switch accounts\n   - Per brief frame 4:2: design a one-page desktop portfolio (1440 wide, dark mode) for full-stack software engineer \"ABM\", single frame named exactly `01_Home`, navigation scrolls to sections (no inter-frame prototype links), all other buttons/links are entry-only\n   - Fixed: frame name, all copy/data verbatim, brand accents #D5491D and #1373D1, typeface Poppins, media assets, default Button. Everything else (colors, type scale, spacing, radii, states, components) is designer's choice\n   - Build reusable components for all states (hover, current nav) and business components (header, footer, nav, avatar block, tech logo row, project card, experience entry with company mark, contact block)\n   - Process requirements: Reasoning summary: prefix before every tool call; use get_screenshot to verify all screens; finish required screens/states/prototype flows; final answer must include file URL, workspace page ID, screen IDs, prototype work completed, limitations\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Figma Plugin API via use_figma tool (50000 char limit per call), figma.setCurrentPageAsync, loadFontAsync (Poppins styles: 'Regular','Medium','SemiBold','Bold' — \"SemiBold\" not \"Semi Bold\")\n   - combineAsVariants for component sets; instance overrides (text characters, fills allowed; size/rescale NOT overridable on nested instances)\n   - swapComponent avoided in favor of fills override with imageHash (`{type:'IMAGE', scaleMode:'FILL', imageHash}`) for photo swapping\n   - Prototype Reaction schema (learned through errors): `{trigger:{type:'ON_CLICK'|'MOUSE_ENTER'|'MOUSE_LEAVE', delay:0}, actions:[{type:'NODE', destinationId, navigation:'SCROLL_TO'|'CHANGE_TO'|'NAVIGATE'|'SWAP'|'OVERLAY', transition:{type:'SMART_ANIMATE', duration, easing:{type:'EASE_OUT'}}}]}` — uses `actions` array (not `action`), trigger `ON_CLICK` (not CLICK), navigation `SCROLL_TO` (not SCROLL), CHANGE_TO is a navigation value under type NODE\n   - Auto-layout: maxWidth/layoutAlign must be set after appendChild; async layout means height reads can be stale immediately after creation\n   - Helpers: hex→rgb converter, solid paint, gradient paint (GRADIENT_LINEAR with gradientTransform [[0,1,0],[-1,0,1]]), recursive recolor of vector children\n   - Design tokens chosen: page bg #0C0C10, surface #14141A, tile #121218, borders #22222A/#23232B/#26262E/#2A2A33/#1E1E26, text #FFFFFF/#A3A3B2/#6E6E7E, accents #D5491D/#1373D1, hover orange #E2582A, date blue tint #5AA2EC, logo recolor #E8E8EE; H1 46 SemiBold lh125%, section title 36, body 16 Regular lh170%, eyebrow 14 SemiBold ls3px, caption 12 SemiBold ls2.4px, nav 16 Medium\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - Figma file embiTe5NXuX0R3PKHD3OV7 pages: 0:1 (brief), 1:2 (foundations), 1:3 (components), 1:4 (media), 5:2 (workspace — all work here)\n   - Media source components (read-only, instanced): Logo_ABM 3:4 (169×96, single IMAGE-fill node), Photo_Avatar 3:13, Photo_Project_CSS 3:14, Photo_Project_HTML 3:15, Logo_CSS3 3:5, Logo_HTML5 3:6, Logo_JavaScript 3:8, Logo_Nextjs 3:9, Logo_React 3:10, Logo_Instagram 3:7, Logo_X 3:11, Logo_YouTube 3:12, Icon_Arrow_Up_Right 3:2, Icon_Mail 3:3\n   - **Created in Workspace (components area at x=-1800):**\n     - Button set 7:10 — variants: 7:2 Primary Default (#D5491D fill, white text), 7:4 Primary Hover (#E2582A), 7:6 Secondary Default (#14141A fill, #3A3A46 stroke), 7:8 Secondary Hover (#1C1C25 fill, #D5491D stroke). Pill radius 100, padding 36/16, Poppins SemiBold 16, text child named 'Label'\n     - Nav_Item set 8:11 — 8:2 Default (#A3A3B2), 8:5 Hover (#FFFFFF), 8:8 Current (#FFFFFF + 4×4 #D5491D dot). Vertical autolayout, padding 6/2, spacing 6\n     - Nav_Bar component 8:12 (1440 wide, SPACE_BETWEEN, padding 140/20, fill #0C0C10 92%, bottom stroke #22222A) — logo instance 8:13 (rescale 0.5 → 84.5×48), Nav row 8:14, items: 8:15 Home(Current), 8:18 Projects, 8:21 Experience, 8:24 Contact\n     - Avatar_Block 11:26 (360×360, radius 28, #17171E, stroke #2A2A33, dual DROP_SHADOW: #D5491D a0.28 offset(-28,-28) r90 and #1373D1 a0.28 offset(28,28) r90) with Photo_Avatar rescaled 1.8\n     - Tech_Item set 13:42 — 5 variants Logo=JavaScript/Nextjs/HTML5/CSS3/React (112×112 tiles, radius 20, #121218 fill, #23232B stroke, logo rescaled to h48 inside component, recolored #E8E8EE)\n     - Project_Card 13:61 — 564 wide vertical, radius 20, #14141A, Photo wrapper 564×300 clipsContent with Photo_Project_HTML instance rescaled to 564 wide; Body (padding 28/26/30, gap 10): Caption \"CLICK HERE TO VISIT\" (#D5491D), Title Row with Title \"HTML TUTORIAL\" 22 SemiBold + Arrow 44×44 circle with Icon_Arrow_Up_Right recolored white\n     - Company_Mark set 14:67 — 72×72 radius 18 gradient marks: S (orange #E8734A→#D5491D), MS (blue #4D9FE8→#1373D1), OC (orange→#7A3EC8→blue), initials 24 SemiBold white\n     - Experience_Item 14:68 — horizontal spacing 28, 1160 fixed: Mark instance + Content (Role 20 SemiBold white with \" at ...\" range #A3A3B2; Dates 14 Medium #5AA2EC; Description 15 Regular lh170% #A3A3B2)\n     - Social_Button 15:80 (52×52 circle, #14141A, #26262E stroke, Instagram logo recolored #E8E8EE)\n     - Contact_Block 15:83 (Title \"Contact\" 36; Bio centered 16/170% #A3A3B2; Email pill with Icon_Mail recolored #D5491D at h20 + \"abm@example.com\" 16 Medium; Socials row gap 16)\n     - Footer_Bar 15:101 (1160 wide: 1px divider #1E1E26 + Row SPACE_BETWEEN with Logo_ABM rescale 0.35 + \"© 2026 ABM. All rights reserved.\" 14 #6E6E7E)\n   - **01_Home frame 11:10** (1440 wide, vertical autolayout, #0C0C10, clipsContent false) with children:\n     - Header instance 11:11\n     - Hero \"Home\" section 11:28 (padding 140/80/110, SPACE_BETWEEN): Hero Content col (640 fixed, gap 28): H1 \"I do code and make content about it!\" 46 SemiBold with \"code\" #D5491D and \"content\" #1373D1 range fills; Bio 16/170% #A3A3B2; Actions row: 11:33 = Primary \"Get In Touch\", 11:35 = Secondary \"Download CV\"; avatar instance 11:37\n     - \"Tech Stack\" 13:43 (eyebrow \"EXPERIENCE WITH\" #6E6E7E ls3 + 5 Tech_Item instances gap 32)\n     - \"Projects\" 13:71 (Title 36 + Cards row gap 32: 13:74 HTML default, 13:84 CSS via nested photo fills override `[{type:'IMAGE', scaleMode:'FILL', imageHash: cssHash}]` from 3:14 + Title override \"CSS TUTORIAL\")\n     - \"Experience\" 14:75 (Title 36 + Entries list gap 40 with instances 14:78/14:86/14:94 and 1px dividers #22222A; entries 2/3 override nested mark fills to blue/mixed gradients and Initials to \"MS\"/\"OC\"; all role/dates/description text verbatim from brief including curly apostrophes)\n     - \"Contact\" 15:106 (padding 140/110/48, gap 64, centered: Contact_Block instance 15:107 + Footer_Bar instance 15:125 STRETCH; social instances 15:92/15:95/15:98 with X/YouTube nested recolored)\n   - Key code pattern used throughout:\n     ```js\n     const H = h => { h=h.replace('#',''); return { r: parseInt(h.slice(0,2),16)/255, g: parseInt(h.slice(2,4),16)/255, b: parseInt(h.slice(4,6),16)/255 }; };\n     const S = (hex, opacity=1) => ({ type:'SOLID', color:H(hex), opacity });\n     const HA = (hex,a) => ({...H(hex), a});\n     const G = (stops, tr) => ({ type:'GRADIENT_LINEAR', gradientTransform: tr || [[0,1,0],[-1,0,1]], gradientStops: stops.map(([hex,pos]) => ({position:pos, color:HA(hex,1)})) });\n     const recolor = (node, hex) => { if ('fills' in node && Array.isArray(node.fills) && node.fills.some(f => f.type === 'SOLID')) node.fills = [S(hex)]; if ('children' in node) node.children.forEach(c => recolor(c, hex)); };\n     ```\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - `set_maxWidth: Can only set maxWidth on auto layout nodes and their children` — set maxWidth/layoutAlign BEFORE appendChild; fixed by cleaning up partial nodes and appending first, then setting maxWidth/layoutAlign\n   - Hero text wrapped wrong (h1 3 lines, bio 6 lines) due to hug-width column; fixed by making Hero Content col counterAxisSizingMode FIXED resize(640,10) and texts layoutAlign STRETCH, maxWidth null → h1 640×116 (2 lines), bio 640×81 (3 lines)\n   - `in rescale: This property cannot be overridden in an instance: size` — rescale/resize on nested instances forbidden; fixed by: (a) Tech_Item as component set with 5 variants where rescale+recolor happen inside components; (b) CSS project photo via imageHash fill override on nested instance instead of swapComponent+rescale\n   - Reaction schema errors (3 iterations): (1) trigger 'CLICK' invalid → must be 'ON_CLICK'; navigation 'SCROLL' invalid → 'SCROLL_TO'; CHANGE_TO is not an action type but a navigation under {type:'NODE'}; (2) \"Please update the `actions` field instead of the `action` field\" → use actions array; (3) MOUSE_ENTER/MOUSE_LEAVE triggers require `delay` property (delay:0)\n   - UNRESOLVED (current): nav reactions on 8:15/8:18/8:21/8:24 (nested instances inside Nav_Bar component 8:12) fail with \"Reaction at index 0 was invalid\" for the ON_CLICK SCROLL_TO reaction; button hover reactions on 11:33/11:35: MOUSE_ENTER→hover variant passes but MOUSE_LEAVE→default variant (7:2/7:6) rejected with \"destination 7:2 was rejected — the destination node may not exist, the source may not be a valid prototype source, or the destination may not be reachable from this source\" (likely because destination = currently-active variant, i.e., self-transition)\n   - Stale async layout reads (homeH read 987 right after build; actual taller) — verify via screenshot instead\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - All six sections built with verbatim copy/data; component reuse established (instances of media components + own component sets)\n   - Third-party logos recolored from #1A1A1F to #E8E8EE via recursive fills override on instance children\n   - Ongoing: prototype reactions. Planned fixes to try: (a) use ON_HOVER trigger for hover variant switching (Figma's \"while hovering\" auto-reverts, avoiding self-destination rejection); (b) for nav SCROLL_TO: try setting reactions on the nav item instances inside the header INSTANCE in the main frame (children of 11:11) instead of inside the component, and/or omit transition or use a different transition for SCROLL_TO\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Initial task message (Chinese): “请在以下Figma文件中完成完整设计：Figma 文件：https://www.figma.com/design/embiTe5NXuX0R3PKHD3OV7/ 请先阅读「00·Start Here」中的设计任务，参考「01· Foundations」中的视觉规范，复用「02·Components」中的组件，使用「04·Media」中的素材，最终将完整设计交付至「03·Workspace」。\"\n   - (Accompanying system instructions: whoami before writing and confirm account zhengyaozhi@tetras.ai; preserve reference pages; \"Reasoning summary:\" before every tool call and after each tool result; final response starts 'Reasoning summary: ...' then 'Final answer:'; unattended session — resolve routine choices using the brief; report actual limitations if blocked; no emojis; finish required screens/states/prototype flows before final answer)\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Fix prototype interactions: nav items (Home/Projects/Experience/Contact) scroll to sections (11:28, 13:71, 14:75, 15:106); hover states for nav items (8:2↔8:5) and hero buttons (7:2↔7:4, 7:6↔7:8) — current attempt failed, needs retry with corrected approach\n   - Screenshot verification of full 01_Home frame and components; fix visible visual problems (layout heights never visually verified yet; tech logo recoloring, avatar, gradients, spacing all need visual check)\n   - Possibly re-verify section heights/frame structure after all async layout settles\n   - Final answer with: assigned file URL, Workspace page ID (5:2), screen/frame IDs (01_Home 11:10 and section IDs), prototype work summary, remaining limitations\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Adding prototype reactions via use_figma. The last call attempted:\n   ```js\n   nav.reactions = [{trigger:{type:'ON_CLICK'}, actions:[{type:'NODE', destinationId: destId, navigation:'SCROLL_TO', transition:{type:'SMART_ANIMATE', duration:0.8, easing:{type:'EASE_OUT'}}}]}, ...hover reactions with MOUSE_ENTER/MOUSE_LEAVE delay:0 CHANGE_TO 8:5/8:2...]\n   ```\n   Result: all four nav items failed with \"Reaction at index 0 was invalid\" (the ON_CLICK SCROLL_TO reaction), and both hero buttons failed at \"Reaction at index 1 was invalid (destination 7:2 was rejected...)\" / \"(destination 7:6 was rejected...)\" — i.e., MOUSE_ENTER→hover variant (index 0) validated OK, but MOUSE_LEAVE→the currently-active default variant was rejected as a destination. Nav destinations used: 8:15→11:28 (Home/hero), 8:18→13:71 (Projects), 8:21→14:75 (Experience), 8:24→15:106 (Contact). Buttons: 11:33 (7:2↔7:4), 11:35 (7:6↔7:8).\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Debug and fix the reactions. Direct evidence of where I left off: errors `\"8:15: in set_reactions: Reaction at index 0 was invalid\"` and `\"btn: in set_reactions: Reaction at index 1 was invalid (destination 7:2 was rejected — ...)\"`. Plan: (1) test SCROLL_TO without transition / with simpler transition, and try setting the nav reactions on the nested nav instances inside the header instance 11:11 in the main frame (rather than inside Nav_Bar component 8:12) to see if context resolves the rejection; (2) for hover states, try trigger `{type:'ON_HOVER'}` with CHANGE_TO to the hover variant (auto-reverts on leave, avoiding self-destination rejection); if ON_HOVER is invalid, keep MOUSE_ENTER→hover and find an accepted way for revert (e.g., MOUSE_LEAVE with delay or re-adding after the enter reaction exists). After reactions are in place, take get_screenshot of 11:10 (full 01_Home) plus section-level screenshots, fix any visual issues found, then deliver the final answer per the required format.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /mnt/afs/huangxinyue/bench-runs/web10-main-v4-20261102/runs/TEST-040_1793585508181/claude-config/projects/-mnt-afs-huangxinyue-bench-runs-web10-main-v4-20261102-workspace/f27098c1-0b8f-45bd-83b8-e941b77614a9.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f27098c1-0b8f-45bd-83b8-e941b77614a9","uuid":"36b93b23-a6ec-4fdb-99d4-7e3cc4a491dc","timestamp":"2026-11-02T02:34:36.974Z","isSynthetic":true}
