t index 0 was invalid\" (a post-validation semantic check, not schema). So schema-wise NODE+transition passes, but semantically SCROLL_TO with SMART_ANIMATE rejected.\n\nWhat transition does SCROLL_TO accept? In Figma UI, scroll-to has option \"Instant\" or animation. The API type for scroll transitions: `ScrollToTransition`? There's `{type:'SCROLL_ANIMATION'}`? Hmm. In the plugin API docs, Transition: {type:'DISSOLVE'|'SMART_ANIMATE'|'MOVE_IN'|'MOVE_OUT'|'PUSH'|'SLIDE_IN'|'SLIDE_OUT'} plus direction/easing/duration. For scroll_to, the UI offers \"Instant\" or \"Animated\". Maybe for SCROLL_TO, transition must be `{type:'INSTANT'}`? There is an InstantTransition? Hmm, not sure. Let me try transition {type:'INSTANT'} — hmm, is 'INSTANT' a valid transition type? In recent plugin API: `InstantTransition { type: 'INSTANT' }`? I believe yes, newer API added {type:'INSTANT'}.\n\nActually wait — reconsider. Maybe the semantic rejection \"Reaction at index 0 was invalid\" was because destination 11:28 is not \"reachable\" — for SCROLL_TO from a node nested inside a component instance in 01_Home, destination must be within the same top-level frame context. 8:15 is inside component 8:12, whose instance is in 01_Home. The reaction defined on the component's child applies to instances. Destination 11:28 is a child of 01_Home — but from the component's perspective, the prototype flow starts at top-level frames containing instances of 8:12. Hmm.\n\nBetter approach: set the scroll reactions on the nav item instances INSIDE the header instance in 01_Home (children of 11:11). Those are actual nodes in the flow. Let me find them: 11:11 is INSTANCE of 8:12. Its children include an instance of 8:14 (nav row) with children instances of 8:2-variant Nav_Item. Set reactions there. For SCROLL_TO with transition {type:'SMART_ANIMATE'}... The original error with transition was \"Reaction at index 0 was invalid\" — same message that destination rejection gives. So possibly destination unreachable from component. From instance-in-flow, should be fine.\n\nAlso try {type:'INSTANT'} if SMART_ANIMATE fails. Let me first find nested nav ids in header instance 11:11.","signature":"628498c8e5184971938944b0"}],"id":"9f86ad54-7bf0-4bc7-ab6b-34f4d6bdf4ea","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f27098c1-0b8f-45bd-83b8-e941b77614a9","uuid":"049ace1a-ab4a-498d-a61a-2ab3ca6bb14d","timestamp":"2026-11-02T02:35:27.076Z","thinking_duration_ms":28352}
