xt.\n5. Verify.\n\nFor setProperties on instance with variant: property name is \"Logo\" (from \"Logo=Instagram\" naming). But careful: 15:95/98 currently instances of 15:80 with nested overrides; setProperties changes variant — overrides on swapped layers reset; fine.\n\ncombineAsVariants(nodes, parent) — parent: the page/current parent. Place set at same location: set.x = 15:80.x, set.y = 15:80.y (roughly). Components are at components area x=-1800. Get soc.x/y first.\n\nNew components: figma.createComponent() 52x52; fills #14141A; cornerRadius 26; strokes #26262E strokeWeight 1; logo instance: figma.createComponent? No — create INSTANCE: const inst = compLogo.createInstance(); rescale(inst, factor); append to button; set x,y.\n\nComponent names: 'Logo=Instagram' etc. After combineAsVariants, set.name = 'Social_Button'.\n\nThen instance.setProperties({'Logo': 'X'}) — actually for setProperties the key is the variant property name 'Logo'. Might error if property not found until set exists — it will exist.\n\nTech row reorder: row = 13:45; children [13:46 JS,13:49 Next,13:52 HTML5,13:55 CSS3,13:58 React]. Desired order: [13:52 HTML5, 13:55 CSS3, 13:46 JS, 13:58 React, 13:49 Next]. Use row.insertChild(index, child) sequentially.\n\nOne script; careful with size (<50k). Then screenshot the tech+contact region only? Screenshot full frame again at end.","signature":"d311c420020f4ef0adf0dc12"}],"id":"03c12028-037e-413f-9033-c726d35dc9e2","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f27098c1-0b8f-45bd-83b8-e941b77614a9","uuid":"a4d094a2-4026-4fc9-9f99-69ddb8a2c45f","timestamp":"2026-11-02T02:48:27.385Z","thinking_duration_ms":27545}
